          "kind": "class",
          "description": "Number control. Form-associated: `name` submits `value`, a form reset restores the value from connection, and a disabled fieldset disables the control. Wraps `<input type=\"number\">`, so the spinner, arrow keys, and step behavior stay native. `min`, `max`, and `step` are forwarded. Omit them for the browser defaults: step `1`, no minimum, and no maximum. `value` is the sanitized string. Blank is `\"\"`, which is distinct from `\"0\"`. Enter calls `requestSubmit()` on the parent form unless the control is disabled or readonly. `input` is the inner input event, retargeted to this host after `value` updates. Constraint validity mirrors the inner input, so `checkValidity` and `reportValidity` honor `min`, `max`, `step`, and `required`. `unit` renders after the input and stays visible when help is hidden. No slots. No public methods. `ui-form-field` writes `description`, `described-by`, `invalid`, and `required`.",
